{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Implementation choice:} Use {\f1 swift-markdown} (Apple\u8217's open-source library) to parse Markdown AST, then walk the AST to produce SwiftUI views. Do not use {\f1 WebView} \u8212- this is a native app.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 For Phase 1, syntax highlighting in code blocks is rendered in a fixed monospace font without colorization. Syntax highlighting is a Phase 2 feature.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 3.5 Session Management\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.5.1 Session List\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The sidebar displays a scrollable list of sessions fetched from the gateway via REST:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 GET /api/sessions\line
Authorization: Bearer <token>\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Response: array of session objects (see Section 7.1).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Session list item display:} - Session label or auto-generated name (first message preview) - Last activity timestamp (relative: \u8220"2 min ago\u8221", \u8220"Yesterday\u8221") - Unread indicator dot (for sessions with new messages since last view)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Ordering:} Most recently active first.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Session search:} Text field at top of sidebar filters list in real-time. Searches session labels and first-message previews.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.5.2 Session Selection\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Clicking a session: 1. Load message history from local SQLite (instant) 2. Fetch any messages newer than last cached message from gateway 3. Mark session as active \u8212- subsequent incoming messages routed here\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.5.3 New Session\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8220"+\u8221" button at top of sidebar calls:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 POST /api/sessions\line
Authorization: Bearer <token>\line
Content-Type: application/json\line
\line
\{ "label": null \}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Returns new session object. App selects it immediately, ready to send first message.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 3.6 File Attachments\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.6.1 Drag and Drop\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The chat input area accepts file drops. Drop targets: - The chat message input field - Anywhere in the chat view (fallback)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Drop behavior:} 1. User drags file from Finder into chat area 2. App shows drop preview overlay: filename, icon, size 3. User releases \u8594 ? upload begins 4. Progress indicator appears in the chat input area 5. On upload complete: attachment reference appended to current draft message 6. User sends message \u8594 ? message includes attachment reference\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.6.2 File Upload Protocol\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Files are uploaded to the gateway via HTTPS multipart upload (not WebSocket \u8212- binary file transfer over WebSocket is inefficient and adds complexity):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 POST /api/workspace/upload\line
Authorization: Bearer <token>\line
Content-Type: multipart/form-data\line
\line
--boundary\line
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="document.pdf"\line
Content-Type: application/pdf\line
\line
<binary data>\line
--boundary--\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Response:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 \{\line
  "path": "/root/.openclaw/workspace/uploads/document.pdf",\line
  "size": 204800,\line
  "mime_type": "application/pdf"\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The returned {\f1 path} is included in the chat message payload so the agent can reference it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.6.3 File Size Limits\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Phase 1: 50MB per file. Larger files show an error toast. No multi-file batch upload in Phase 1.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 3.7 Notifications\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.7.1 Notification Trigger Conditions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A notification is sent when: - A new agent response completes (stream ends) - The app window is not the active, front window\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Do NOT send a notification when: - The user is actively viewing the session in a focused window - The app is in foreground\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.7.2 Notification Format\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 Title: "OpenClaw"\line
Subtitle: [Session label or "New Session"]\line
Body: [First 120 characters of response]\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Action:} Clicking notification opens the app, selects the relevant session, scrolls to the new message.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3.7.3 Notification Permission\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 On first launch (after connection setup), request notification permission:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 UNUserNotificationCenter.current().requestAuthorization(\line
    options: [.alert, .sound, .badge]\line
) \{ granted, error in ... \}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If denied: show informational banner in the app (\u8220"Notifications disabled. Enable in System Settings \u8594 ? Notifications \u8594 ? OpenClaw\u8221").\par}
