{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Clicking the indicator in {\f1 disconnected} or {\f1 error} state triggers a manual reconnect attempt.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 3.9 Auto-Reconnect\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Reconnect logic:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 On connection drop:\line
  state = .reconnecting\line
  attempt = 0\line
  \line
  loop:\line
    wait(min(60, 2^attempt) seconds)\line
    try connect()\line
    if connected: break\line
    attempt += 1\line
    \line
  if attempt > 10 and still disconnected:\line
    state = .disconnected  // stop retrying, require manual\line
    post notification: "OpenClaw disconnected from gateway"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Network awareness:} Use {\f1 NWPathMonitor} (Network framework) to detect network availability. Do not attempt reconnects when network is unavailable. Resume reconnect loop when network becomes available.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 4. Full Product Specification \u8212- Phase 2+\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Phase 2 builds on the MVP to deliver the full vision: real-time agent transparency, rich workspace management, multi-gateway support, and platform integrations.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.1 Three-Pane Layout\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The default window layout in Phase 2 is three vertical panes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 +------------------+------------------------+---------------------+\line
| SIDEBAR          | CHAT                   | WORK PANEL          |\line
| (240px min)      | (flexible, 400px min)  | (320px min)         |\line
|                  |                        |                     |\line
| Sessions         | Message thread         | Live tool calls     |\line
| Agents           | Input area             | Subagent status     |\line
| Connections      |                        | File ops timeline   |\line
|                  |                        | Task board          |\line
+------------------+------------------------+---------------------+\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Panes are resizable via drag handles. The Work Panel can be collapsed (hidden) when not needed. The sidebar can also be collapsed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 User pane sizes are persisted in {\f1 UserDefaults}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.2 Work Panel \u8212- Live Task Board\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The Work Panel provides real-time visibility into what the agent is doing while generating a response.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 4.2.1 Event Stream\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The gateway emits structured events over the WebSocket alongside message tokens. These events describe agent activity:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 \{\line
  "type": "agent_event",\line
  "event_kind": "tool_call",\line
  "tool": "Read",\line
  "args": \{ "file_path": "/root/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md" \},\line
  "status": "running",\line
  "timestamp": 1740499200\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Event kinds: - {\f1 tool_call} \u8212- tool invocation started/completed/failed - {\f1 subagent_spawn} \u8212- subagent created - {\f1 subagent_complete} \u8212- subagent finished - {\f1 file_read} \u8212- file read operation - {\f1 file_write} \u8212- file write operation - {\f1 web_search} \u8212- web search issued - {\f1 thinking} \u8212- agent is reasoning (optional, if exposed) - {\f1 approval_request} \u8212- agent requests user approval\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 4.2.2 Work Panel Display\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each event renders as a compact card in the Work Panel:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 +----------------------------------------+\line
| \u55357 ?\u56615 ? Read                         2s ago |\line
| /root/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md    |\line
| \u10003 ? 142 lines read                       |\line
+----------------------------------------+\line
\line
+----------------------------------------+\line
| \u55356 ?\u57104 ? Web Search                  running |\line
| "OpenClaw WebSocket protocol"          |\line
| \u10251 ? Fetching results...                  |\line
+----------------------------------------+\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Events animate in from the bottom. Completed events fade slightly. Running events show a spinner. Failed events show in red with error detail.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Card click:} Expands to show full args/result inline.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 4.2.3 Task Board Mode\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A toggle in the Work Panel switches from \u8220"Event Stream\u8221" (chronological) to \u8220"Task Board\u8221" (status-grouped):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Running:} Currently executing operations\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Completed:} Finished this session\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Failed:} Operations that errored\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.3 Timeline Replay\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The Timeline Replay feature allows scrubbing through the history of an agent task like a video.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Access:} A timeline scrubber appears at the bottom of the Work Panel for completed sessions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Behavior:} - Scrubbing the timeline replays Work Panel events in chronological order - The chat view syncs \u8212- messages appear/disappear as if watching it happen in real time - Play/pause controls - Speed control: 1x, 2x, 4x, 8x\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Data source:} All events are persisted in SQLite (see Section 7.3). Replay reads from local store only.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Use case:} Understanding why an agent made a particular decision, auditing actions after the fact, sharing agent \u8220"runs\u8221" as recordings.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.4 Agent Roster\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A panel (accessible from the sidebar or a dedicated tab) showing all agents managed by the connected gateway.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Per-agent display:} - Agent name and label - Status: active / idle / error - Active session count - Memory size (approximate token count) - Last activity timestamp - Memory summary stats (from gateway)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Actions available per agent:} - View agent configuration - View memory (read-only in Phase 2, editable in Phase 3) - View active sessions - Kill active session\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Data source:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 GET /api/agents\line
Authorization: Bearer <token>\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Refreshed every 30 seconds and on WebSocket events.\par}
