Authorization: Bearer <token>\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.6 Steer Controls\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When an agent is actively responding, the Work Panel shows a Steer toolbar:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 [\u9208 ? Pause]  [\u9209 ? Stop]  [\u8617 ? Redirect]\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Pause:} Sends a pause signal to the gateway. Agent completes current tool call and waits.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Stop:} Sends a stop signal. Agent stops after current operation, outputs partial result.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Redirect:} Opens a text field inline. User types a new instruction. Sent as a steer message to the gateway mid-task.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Protocol:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 \{\line
  "type": "steer",\line
  "action": "pause" | "stop" | "redirect",\line
  "message": "Focus only on the billing module, skip auth",\line
  "session_id": "abc123"\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.7 Approval Flows\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When the agent encounters an action requiring human approval (defined by gateway policy), it emits an {\f1 approval_request} event:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 \{\line
  "type": "approval_request",\line
  "request_id": "req_abc123",\line
  "action": "exec",\line
  "description": "Run shell command: rm -rf /tmp/old_cache",\line
  "risk_level": "medium",\line
  "timeout_seconds": 120\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b In-app:} An approval card appears in the Work Panel with Approve/Deny buttons.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Notification:} If the app is not focused, a macOS actionable notification is delivered:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 Title: "OpenClaw \u8212- Action Required"\line
Body: "Agent wants to: rm -rf /tmp/old_cache"\line
Actions: [Approve] [Deny]\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The user can approve or deny directly from the notification without opening the app.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Timeout:} If not responded to within {\f1 timeout_seconds}, the gateway auto-denies and the agent is notified.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Response protocol:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 \{\line
  "type": "approval_response",\line
  "request_id": "req_abc123",\line
  "approved": true,\line
  "note": null\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.8 Multi-Gateway Support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The app supports connecting to multiple OpenClaw gateways simultaneously (e.g., personal VPS, work server).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Gateway model:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 struct Gateway \{\line
    var id: UUID\line
    var label: String        // "Home Server", "Work VPS"\line
    var url: URL\line
    var tokenRef: String     // Keychain reference, not the token itself\line
    var isActive: Bool\line
    var lastConnected: Date?\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b UI:} A gateway picker at the top of the sidebar (dropdown or segmented control). Switching changes the active gateway \u8212- sessions, agents, and artifacts all update.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Simultaneous connections:} App maintains WebSocket connections to all configured gateways. Notifications arrive from all. Active gateway determines what\u8217's displayed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b iCloud sync of gateway configs:} Gateway URLs and labels sync via {\f1 NSUbiquitousKeyValueStore}. Tokens do NOT sync \u8212- they are Keychain-bound to the local device.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.9 Spotlight-Style Summon\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A global keyboard shortcut (default: {\f1 \u8963 ?Space}, user-configurable) summons a command palette overlay:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 +--------------------------------------------------+\line
| > _                                              |\line
+--------------------------------------------------+\line
| Recent Sessions                                  |\line
|   \u55357 ?\u56492 ?  Debug the billing module (2 min ago)       |\line
|   \u55357 ?\u56492 ?  Weekly planning session (1 hour ago)       |\line
| Quick Actions                                    |\line
|   \u10024 ?  New Chat Session                           |\line
|   \u55357 ?\u56589 ?  Search All Sessions                        |\line
|   \u55357 ?\u56514 ?  Open Artifact Library                      |\line
+--------------------------------------------------+\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Behavior:} - Registered via {\f1 Carbon.framework} {\f1 EventHotKey} API (for global, system-wide shortcut) - Palette appears above all windows, including full-screen apps - ESC dismisses - Return on a session opens it in the main window - Type to fuzzy search across sessions, agents, artifacts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.10 Command Palette (\u8984 ?K)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Within the app (window focused), \u8984 ?K opens a command palette similar to Linear or Raycast:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Sessions:} Switch to any session by name\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Agents:} Jump to agent in roster\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Artifacts:} Open any file by path\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Actions:} New session, disconnect, export conversation, open settings\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Steer commands:} Pause, stop, redirect current task\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Fuzzy search across all categories. Keyboard-navigable.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.11 Apple Watch Companion\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A watchOS app paired via {\f1 WatchConnectivity} ({\f1 WCSession}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Watch features:} - Glanceable status: which agent is active, what it\u8217's doing (one-line summary) - Approval notifications with Digital Crown scroll to read full action description - Tap-to-approve / tap-to-deny from watch - Brief conversation summary: last message in/out\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Complication:} A small complication showing agent status (idle/active/needs-attention) on watch faces.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Data flow:} macOS app bridges messages to watch via {\f1 WCSession.sendMessage()}. Approvals reverse the flow.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.12 Handoff Support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Implements {\f1 NSUserActivity} so a conversation can be handed off to the iPhone OpenClaw app (future).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Activity type:} {\f1 com.openclaw.session}\line {\b User info:} {\f1 \{ "session_id": "abc123", "gateway_url": "https://..." \}}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The iPhone app (out of scope for this spec) receives the Handoff and opens the same session.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.13 Voice Input\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Integrates macOS dictation via {\f1 SFSpeechRecognizer}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Microphone button in chat input area\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Hold: push-to-talk mode\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Click: toggle on/off\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Live transcription preview in the input field\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Send on release (push-to-talk) or manual send\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Does not require internet \u8212- uses on-device speech recognition where available.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.14 Export Conversation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Export the current session as: - {\b Markdown:} Full conversation thread in {\f1 .md} format - {\b PDF:} Styled PDF via {\f1 PDFDocument} with header, timestamp, session metadata\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Access: File menu \u8594 ? Export, or right-click session in sidebar.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 4.15 Syntax Highlighting\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Code blocks in Phase 2 use a syntax highlighting library (recommend {\f1 Highlightr} \u8212- a Swift wrapper around highlight.js):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Auto-detect language from fenced code block language tag\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fallback to plain monospace for unknown languages\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Two themes: light and dark (follows system appearance)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Language label in top-right corner of code block\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Copy button in code block header\sa180\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 5. Technical Architecture\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 5.1 App Architecture\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The app uses {\b MVVM (Model-View-ViewModel)} with Swift Concurrency ({\f1 async/await}, {\f1 Actor}) for all asynchronous operations. Combine is used for reactive UI bindings where SwiftUI\u8217's native binding is insufficient.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5.1.1 Layer Overview\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 +--------------------------------------------------+\line
|                    SwiftUI Views                 |  \u8592 ? Pure display, zero business logic\line
+--------------------------------------------------+\line
|                   ViewModels                     |  \u8592 ? @ObservableObject, @MainActor\line
+--------------------------------------------------+\line
|                   Services                       |  \u8592 ? Business logic, protocol-oriented\line
+--------------------------------------------------+\line
|   Gateway Client  |  Local Store  |  Keychain    |  \u8592 ? Infrastructure\line
+--------------------------------------------------+\line
|        URLSession / Network.framework / SQLite   |  \u8592 ? System frameworks\line
+--------------------------------------------------+\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5.1.2 Key Services\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b GatewayClient:} Owns the WebSocket connection. Handles connect/disconnect/reconnect, sends messages, receives and parses incoming events. Exposes an {\f1 AsyncSequence} of {\f1 GatewayEvent} values.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b SessionStore:} Manages the SQLite database. CRUD for sessions, messages, artifacts. Provides query methods returning {\f1 AsyncStream<[Session]>} etc. Uses {\f1 @Actor} isolation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b NotificationService:} Evaluates whether to post a notification and calls {\f1 UNUserNotificationCenter}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b KeychainService:} Wraps {\f1 SecItemAdd}/{\f1 SecItemCopyMatching}/{\f1 SecItemUpdate}/{\f1 SecItemDelete}. Typed API \u8212- {\f1 func storeToken(_ token: String, for gateway: URL)}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b FileTransferService:} Handles file uploads via {\f1 URLSession} multipart POST. Exposes {\f1 uploadFile(at url: URL, to gateway: Gateway) async throws -> RemotePath}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b WorkPanelEventProcessor:} Subscribes to {\f1 GatewayClient} events, filters {\f1 agent_event} types, maintains the ordered list of {\f1 WorkEvent} for the Work Panel view.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5.1.3 Concurrency Model\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab All UI updates on {\f1 @MainActor}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 GatewayClient} isolated to a custom {\f1 Actor}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab SQLite operations on a dedicated {\f1 DatabaseActor}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab File uploads on {\f1 Task} with cooperative cancellation support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Reconnect logic runs as a structured {\f1 Task} that observes {\f1 NWPathMonitor}\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5.1.4 State Management\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Top-level state lives in {\f1 AppState} \u8212- an {\f1 ObservableObject} injected into the SwiftUI environment:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 @MainActor\line
final class AppState: ObservableObject \{\line
    @Published var gateways: [Gateway] = []\line
    @Published var activeGateway: Gateway?\line
    @Published var connectionState: ConnectionState = .disconnected\line
    @Published var sessions: [Session] = []\line
    @Published var activeSession: Session?\line
    @Published var workEvents: [WorkEvent] = []\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ViewModels hold view-local state and observe relevant slices of {\f1 AppState}.\par}
