{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 5.4 Local Data Store\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 SQLite database at: {\f1 ~/Library/Application Support/OpenClaw/openclaw.db}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Encrypted with SQLCipher using a key stored in Keychain (see Section 8.3).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Database access uses {\f1 GRDB.swift} (a well-maintained, Swift-native SQLite library). GRDB provides type-safe queries, migrations, and {\f1 ValueObservation} for reactive updates.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5.4.1 Dependency rationale\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 GRDB.swift} is preferred over raw SQLite3 because: - Type-safe Codable record mapping - ValueObservation integrates cleanly with SwiftUI via Combine - Built-in migration support - Active maintenance, MIT license\par}
