{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 8. Security Model\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 8.1 Transport Security\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 All communication between the macOS app and the gateway uses TLS 1.2 minimum (TLS 1.3 preferred).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The gateway runs behind Tailscale. Tailscale provides mutual device authentication and encrypted overlay networking \u8212- only authorized devices on the Tailscale network can reach the gateway at all.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The HTTPS/WSS certificate is validated by the system trust store. Certificate pinning is NOT implemented in Phase 1 \u8212- Tailscale\u8217's network isolation is considered sufficient. Certificate pinning can be added in Phase 2 if required.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab App Transport Security (ATS) is enabled. No HTTP (non-TLS) connections are permitted.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 8.2 Keychain Storage\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Auth tokens and database encryption keys are stored in the macOS Keychain, not in UserDefaults, plist files, or the filesystem.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Keychain schema:}\par}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\clbrdrb\brdrs\cellx2160\clbrdrb\brdrs\cellx4320\clbrdrb\brdrs\cellx6480\clbrdrb\brdrs\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Item\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Service\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Account\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Description\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Gateway auth token\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 com.openclaw.gateway-token}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Gateway URL (e.g.\u160 ?{\f1 https://ubuntu-ct...})\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Bearer token for gateway auth\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 DB encryption key\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 com.openclaw.db-key}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 local}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 32-byte random key for SQLCipher\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Access control:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 let accessControl = SecAccessControlCreateWithFlags(\line
    nil,\line
    kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly,\line
    .userPresence,  // Require biometric/password for sensitive items\line
    nil\line
)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly}: Items not backed up to iCloud, not transferred to new device\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Gateway tokens require {\f1 .userPresence} (biometric or password) on first access per session\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab DB key does NOT require {\f1 .userPresence} (accessed frequently, would be unusable)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Keychain API wrapper:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 final class KeychainService \{\line
    func store(_ value: String, service: String, account: String) throws\line
    func retrieve(service: String, account: String) throws -> String\line
    func update(_ value: String, service: String, account: String) throws\line
    func delete(service: String, account: String) throws\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 All Keychain errors are typed ({\f1 KeychainError}) and handled \u8212- never silently ignored.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 8.3 Database Encryption\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The local SQLite database is encrypted using SQLCipher (AES-256-CBC) via the {\f1 SQLCipher} Swift package.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The encryption key is a 32-byte random value generated on first launch and stored in Keychain (see Section 8.2).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 var config = Configuration()\line
config.prepareDatabase \{ db in\line
    let key = try KeychainService.shared.retrieve(service: "com.openclaw.db-key", account: "local")\line
    try db.usePassphrase(key)\line
\}\line
let dbQueue = try DatabaseQueue(path: dbPath, configuration: config)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If the Keychain item is unavailable (e.g., user locked Mac, biometric unavailable), the database is not opened and a lock screen is displayed. Chat history is accessible only when the Mac is unlocked.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 8.4 Token Handling in Memory\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Auth token is loaded from Keychain into memory at connection time as a {\f1 String}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab It is passed to {\f1 GatewayClient} as a parameter and stored in the actor\u8217's private state\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab It is NOT stored in any {\f1 UserDefaults}, {\f1 AppState} @Published properties, or view models\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab It is NOT logged anywhere (no debug logging of Authorization headers)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab It is zeroed in memory when the gateway disconnects or the app quits (use {\f1 withUnsafeMutableBytes} + {\f1 memset})\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 8.5 No Telemetry\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The app collects no usage data, crash reports, or analytics. There are no third-party SDKs for analytics, crash reporting, or feature flags. Error logging is local only (OSLog, accessible via Console.app).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If crash reporting is desired in the future, use only Apple\u8217's built-in crash reporter via the App Store, which is opt-in and user-controlled.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 8.6 File Upload Security\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Uploaded files are sent to the gateway workspace with no server-side sanitization guarantees. The client: - Enforces a 50MB file size limit before upload - Does not execute or preview file content beyond known safe types (images, text, markdown) - For image previews: renders via {\f1 NSImage}/{\f1 Image}, not via a web view - Never auto-executes uploaded scripts or executables\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 8.7 macOS Sandbox\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The app runs in the macOS App Sandbox with the following entitlements:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>\line
<true/>\line
\line
<!-- Network access to gateway -->\line
<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>\line
<true/>\line
\line
<!-- User-selected file access for attachments -->\line
<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only</key>\line
<true/>\line
\line
<!-- Notifications -->\line
<key>com.apple.security.user-notifications</key>\line
<true/>\line
\line
<!-- Keychain -->\line
<key>keychain-access-groups</key>\line
<array>\line
    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.openclaw</string>\line
</array>\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 No {\f1 com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.absolute-path} or other sandbox escapes. File access outside the app container is gated on user-initiated open panels.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
