{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 9.5 Signing & Entitlements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Development:} Personal team signing for local dev\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Distribution:} Developer ID Application certificate (for direct distribution outside App Store)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Notarization:} Required for distribution outside App Store (macOS Gatekeeper). Use {\f1 altool} or {\f1 notarytool} in CI pipeline.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Hardened Runtime:} Enabled for notarization. Required entitlements explicitly declared (see Section 8.7).\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 9.6 Distribution Strategy\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Phase 1:} Direct download. Distribute as a notarized {\f1 .dmg} via: - GitHub Releases (if open source) - A private download URL (if closed)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Auto-update:} Implement {\f1 Sparkle 2} for automatic updates. Update feed hosted alongside the app binary. Update check on launch and every 24 hours. User can disable auto-check in Settings.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Phase 2+:} Evaluate Mac App Store submission. App Store distribution simplifies update delivery but requires: - iCloud entitlements for config sync - No direct network connections to arbitrary URLs (may conflict with gateway URL configurability \u8212- needs review) - App Review timeline\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Recommended: Maintain Developer ID distribution as primary, App Store as secondary if required by enterprise users.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 9.7 CI/CD\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Recommended pipeline (GitHub Actions):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 # On push to main\line
jobs:\line
  build:\line
    runs-on: macos-14          # Apple Silicon runner\line
    steps:\line
      - checkout\line
      - xcodebuild test        # Unit tests + UI tests\line
      - xcodebuild archive     # Release build\line
      - xcrun notarytool       # Notarization\line
      - create dmg             # Package\line
      - upload release         # GitHub Release\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Build matrix: run {\f1 xcodebuild test} on both {\f1 x86_64} (Intel runner) and {\f1 arm64} (Apple Silicon runner) to catch architecture-specific issues.\par}
